{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-q-jacobiator","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:q-jacobiator","kind":"proposition","title":"Jacobiator of the q-Lie bracket","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-q-lie-bracket"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-q-jacobiator"],"tags":["q-deformation","lie-bracket","leibniz-algebra"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.q_jacobiator","text":"q-jacobiator.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-jacobiator.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:q-jacobiator\"></a><p>The archimedean specialisation violates the Jacobi identity for horizontal vector fields when <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\neq 1</code>. The Jacobiator reads</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathrm{Jac}_q(U,V,W) = -q^{-1}(1-q^{-1})\\!\\sum_{\\mathrm{cyc}} d\\varTheta(V,W)\\mathcal{L}_\\xi U.</code></pre>\n<p>Since the Levi form <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d\\varTheta|_{H \\times H}</code> is non-degenerate, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathfrak{X}(M), [\\cdot,\\cdot]_q)</code> forms a Leibniz algebra.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-jacobiator.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Proposition","number":"3.26.2"}
